cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GeulPU in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GeulPU: a deterministic local LLM engine and debugger"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Woo"
    given-names: "Sunghyeun"
    affiliation: "Chungwoon University"
    alias: "wwoosshh"
    website: "https://github.com/wwoosshh"
version: "0.10.1"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23548056"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wwoosshh/GeulPUv2"
url: "https://github.com/wwoosshh/GeulPUv2"
abstract: >-
  GeulPU runs GGUF language models on a local GPU with output that is bit-identical to a CPU reference implementation of a written
  precision contract — across batching, slots, the prompt cache, speculative decoding and, in exact mode, CUDA and Vulkan GPUs. Its
  debugger records generation runs, replays them bit for bit, branches from any token or request, and compares runs across model
  files, quantizations and versions. The engine, kernels, server and app are written in the geul programming language.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - local inference
  - reproducibility
  - determinism
  - debugging
  - GGUF
  - CUDA
  - Vulkan
